==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}
===Etymology===
Attested since the 9th century; ultimately from the verb ''[[können]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kʊnst/|[kʰʊnst]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Kunst.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Künste}}

# [[art]]
# {{context|now|_|chiefly|as the first part of compound words|lang=de}} something [[artificial]]ly created or manufactured, as opposed to something natural
#* '''2009''', Dorit Steenhusen, ''Träume Schäume Fieberwahn'', page 75:
#*: Und „wer kann es wirklich unterscheiden, ob sie echt sind oder nur '''Kunst'''? Sie sind so sündhaft teuer,“ hatte sie noch hinzugefügt.
#*:: And "who can really tell, if they are real or only '''artificial (things)'''? They are so terribly expensive," she added.
#: '''''Kunstschnee'''''

